<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Tomsk</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Tomsk is a city on the Tom River in western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/siberia">Siberia</a>, founded as a fortress in 1604 by order of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tsar">Tsar</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/boris-godunov">Boris Godunov</a>. It grew as a trading and administrative centre on the route across Siberia and became known as the 'Siberian <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/athens">Athens</a>' after Tomsk University, the first in Siberia, opened in 1888. It is the capital of Tomsk Oblast.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/tomsk.jpg" alt="Tomsk" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Igor Savin / Игорь Савин · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Tomsk0293.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
